{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>After these things.</b> Wherever אַחַר is said — it is immediately after; אַחֲרֵי — at a distance (Bereshit Rabbah). אַחַר הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה — after this miracle was done for him, that he killed the kings, and he was worried and said: perhaps I have already received reward for all my righteousnesses. Therefore the Omnipresent said to him: אַל תִּירָא אַבְרָם אָנֹכִי מָגֵן לָךְ — from the punishment, that you not be punished for all those souls you killed; and as for your worry about receiving your reward — שְׂכָרְךָ הַרְבֵּה מְאֹד (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:44.018064362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}